# Trendyol Integration — Core

## MCP First
Never use training data for Trendyol API details. Use `TrendyolDeveloperToolsMcpServer`.
- `getEndpoint(endpointKey)` before any code or curl
- `getIntegrationPlan` before broad integration requests
- `searchEndpoints(query)` when endpoint key is unknown

## Validation Before Mutation
- `validateRequest(endpointKey, marketplace)` before any mutation is "ready"
- createProducts / updateUnapprovedProducts: also call `validateProductCategoryAttributes`
- Always pass `marketplace: "TR"` or `"GLOBAL"` explicitly

## Async Awareness
Every mutation returns `batchRequestId` — HTTP 200 ≠ success.
- Poll `getBatchRequestResult` → inspect `items[].status`
- COMPLETED ≠ all items succeeded
- Store results within 4 hours

## Stage First
- Stage: `https://stageapigw.trendyol.com` (default)
- Production: `https://apigw.trendyol.com` (explicit confirmation required)
- Base URL configurable in all generated code — never hardcoded

## Scope (Phase 1)
Product Integration API (TR) · Product Integration V2 API (TR) · International Marketplace Product Integration API